---
description: Working on the devia standard itself
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository **is** the standard. Changes here propagate to every project that runs
`devia init` or `devia sync`, so the bar is the one described in `GOVERNANCE.md`.

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `PRINCIPLES.md` before changing policy; read `MEMORY.md` before changing
   anything about `.devia/`.
2. A rule lives in `rules/<domain>/<ID>.md` with frontmatter: id, title, severity, status,
   domain, priority, source, requirement, validation. Filename equals id; directory equals
   domain.
3. Rule IDs are stable. Supersede, never reuse. Never delete an active MUST without a changelog
   entry and a superseding id.
4. `rules/README.md`, `compliance/COVERAGE.md` and `compliance/TRACEABILITY.md` are generated —
   edit the rule files and run `npm run build:index`.
5. Changing `templates/project/` changes what every adopter receives: same review bar as a MUST,
   plus a changelog note saying whether `devia sync` is enough.
6. The CLI ships with **no runtime dependencies**. Keep it that way, or argue it in an ADR.
7. Before reporting done: `npm run validate`, `npm test`, and
   `node bin/devia.mjs check --root .`.
8. Say what you did not verify.
